      "cluster_id": 5,
      "headline_hint": "India rejects Hague Court of Arbitration ruling on Indus Waters Treaty as illegal and without jurisdiction",
      "section": "india",
      "batch_position": 1,
      "claim_count": 13,
      "distinct_outlets": 4,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 13
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 67,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "India's Ministry of External Affairs rejected an interim award on the Indus Waters Treaty issued by the Court of Arbitration in The Hague, calling the body illegally constituted.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-terms-arbitration-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-illegal/articleshow/133664981.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Permanent Court of Arbitration in The Hague stated that the Indus Waters Treaty remains fully in force and that India had no justification for suspending the pact.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-terms-arbitration-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-illegal/articleshow/133664981.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Permanent Court of Arbitration ruled that India must limit work on a hydroelectric plant under construction in Jammu and Kashmir.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-terms-arbitration-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-illegal/articleshow/133664981.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Permanent Court of Arbitration issued an interim order prohibiting India from constructing certain structures of the Ratle hydroelectric project in Jammu and Kashmir.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095384/india-rejects-international-court-order-on-indus-water-treaty-says-panel-illegally-constituted?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "India placed the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty in abeyance following an April 22 terror attack in Pahalgam, Jammu and Kashmir, which killed 26 people.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095384/india-rejects-international-court-order-on-indus-water-treaty-says-panel-illegally-constituted?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Under the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty, water from the eastern rivers Beas, Ravi, and Sutlej was allocated to India, while water from the western rivers Indus, Chenab, and Jhelum was allocated to Pakistan.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095384/india-rejects-international-court-order-on-indus-water-treaty-says-panel-illegally-constituted?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Since suspending the treaty, India has accelerated work on several hydropower projects in Jammu and Kashmir, including the Ratle and Kishenganga projects.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095384/india-rejects-international-court-order-on-indus-water-treaty-says-panel-illegally-constituted?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Court of Arbitration noted that a World Bank-appointed neutral expert will decide by July 2027 whether construction of Indian hydroelectric plants aligns with the Indus Waters Treaty.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/never-recognised-existence-of-india-rejects-hague-arbitration-court-ruling-on-indus-waters-treaty-11788176314083.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "In June, Chenab Valley Power Projects sought forest land diversion of approximately 197 hectares for the Kirthai Stage-II Hydroelectric Project on the Chenab river.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/never-recognised-existence-of-india-rejects-hague-arbitration-court-ruling-on-indus-waters-treaty-11788176314083.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "India suspended the Indus Waters Treaty in April 2025 as part of measures responding to a Pahalgam terror attack carried out by a proxy of Lashkar-e-Taiba.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/india-rejects-illegal-court-of-arbitrations-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-has-no-jurisdiction-101788175567329.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Pakistan petitioned the Permanent Court of Arbitration in The Hague in March 2026 to determine the legal status of the Indus Waters Treaty.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/india-rejects-illegal-court-of-arbitrations-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-has-no-jurisdiction-101788175567329.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Court of Arbitration prohibited India from concreting the Ratle project dam wall and power intake structure above specified levels until 90 days after the Neutral Expert's decision.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/india-rejects-illegal-court-of-arbitrations-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-has-no-jurisdiction-101788175567329.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Court of Arbitration panel evaluating the Indus Waters Treaty dispute was chaired by Sean D. Murphy of the United States.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/india-rejects-illegal-court-of-arbitrations-award-on-indus-waters-treaty-has-no-jurisdiction-101788175567329.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cluster_id": 6,
      "headline_hint": "Draft voter lists published across states show millions of voter name deletions",
      "section": "india",
      "batch_position": 2,
      "claim_count": 13,
      "distinct_outlets": 2,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 13
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 80,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Draft voter lists published under phase three of the Special Intensive Revision removed 6.15 crore names out of 36.08 crore electors across 16 states and 3 Union Territories.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Out of 36.08 crore electors on the rolls in the phase three revision areas, 29.93 crore names were retained in the draft rolls.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Delhi recorded the highest percentage of voter name deletions in the draft rolls at 32.78 percent.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Maharashtra saw the largest absolute reduction in voters, with 2.06 crore names removed from its draft electoral roll.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Karnataka recorded 1.07 crore voter deletions in its draft electoral list, the second highest in absolute terms.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Karnataka Chief Minister D.K. Shivakumar and Telangana Chief Minister A. Revanth Reddy wrote to Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar raising concerns over massive voter deletions.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "In March, the Supreme Court unanimously upheld the constitutional validity of the Election Commission of India's Special Intensive Revision process.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/draft-voter-lists-see-over-6-crore-deletions-so-far-in-sir-third-phase/article71411677.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "In Maharashtra, draft voter rolls retained 7.7 crore voters after 21.1 percent of the state's previous voter base was excluded.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095385/maharashtra-sir-21-voters-removed-from-draft-electoral-rolls?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Pune district had the highest number of uncollected enumeration forms in Maharashtra at 28.6 lakh, followed by Thane at 28.5 lakh and Mumbai Suburban at 26.5 lakh.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095385/maharashtra-sir-21-voters-removed-from-draft-electoral-rolls?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Voters excluded from Maharashtra's draft rolls can file claims and objections through September 30 ahead of the final roll publication on November 4.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095385/maharashtra-sir-21-voters-removed-from-draft-electoral-rolls?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Delhi's draft voter list deleted 47.7 lakh names, reducing the national capital's electorate by about 33 percent from 1.45 crore to 97.5 lakh.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095373/rush-hour-33-voters-deleted-from-delhi-draft-list-sc-stays-fir-against-mohammed-deepak-more?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "During the Special Intensive Revision in Delhi, Rohini recorded an enumeration form digitisation rate of 83.4 percent, whereas Tughlakabad recorded 52.1 percent.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095371/delhi-sir-one-in-three-voters-removed-from-draft-list?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "cluster_id": 6,
          "text": "Draft rolls removed more than 19 percent of registered voters in Karnataka, 16 percent in Haryana, and 10.8 percent in Andhra Pradesh.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095371/delhi-sir-one-in-three-voters-removed-from-draft-list?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
